  "assessment": [
    "Useful bounded inventory distinguishes missing catalogues, model-only/partial status and post-failure freshness without changing product authority.",
    "Existing helper provides a single-evaluate/single-store-read insertion seam; preserving that suffix and startup race is source-feasible.",
    "Existing VM tests can execute the actual generated expression with an absent startup API and finite DOM/store/clock, not a fabricated output.",
    "Only the new property may catch its own observer error; existing old fields remain observable."
  ],
  "actualSourceReviewObligations": [
    "Assert exactly one cdp.evaluate and one store getState, no send/mutation, and one sampled diagnostic Date.now.",
    "Bound value inspection itself: do not eagerly read all scope values/getters through Object.values before slicing; prove overflow stops inspection.",
    "Bound global provider/model row inspection and timestamp input lengths as well as emitted finite numeric ranges; unknown/invalid inputs must produce only closed output.",
    "Use canonical UTC parsing and exact fetchedAt <= sampledNow < staleAt; age/remaining values do not grant readiness.",
    "Preserve every old returned property, startup optional race, existing ownership/capture deadline/screenshot sequence and all Plan70 test bytes.",
    "Test missing versus model_only/partial_response, expiry equality/future fetch, overflow/invalid shape, absence of distinctive private strings, and getter failure with old snapshot fields intact."
  ],
  "limits": [
